  "id": "mammillary-body",
  "term": "mammillary body",
  "definition": "The mammillary body is a brain structure long linked with memory-related function. Evidence described here suggests its medial and lateral parts belong to partly separate networks, with the medial part more related to memory and the lateral part more related to spatial navigation.",
